 - **[React](https://react.dev/)**: Used for UI components.
 - **[Tailwind CSS](https://tailwindcss.com/)**: For styling the application.
 - **[Astro DB](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/database/)**: Powers the comments feature, using a libSQL-compatible database.
+
+## Account settings and passkeys
+
+Successful password sign-in now stores the login API's bearer token in the server-side Astro session and opens `/devtools-times/account/settings`. Tokens are never returned to client-side code. The Node adapter supplies file-backed sessions by default; deployments with multiple instances should configure shared session storage.
+
+The existing sample authentication service does not expose passkey management. Set the server environment variable `PASSKEY_API_URL` to an authentication service that implements the following contract. Without it, account settings show an unavailable message rather than an invented list of keys.
+
+- `GET {PASSKEY_API_URL}/passkeys`: return the signed-in user's complete registered credential list.
+- `PATCH {PASSKEY_API_URL}/passkeys/{credentialId}`: accept `{ "displayName": "My laptop" }` (1–64 characters after trimming).
+- `DELETE {PASSKEY_API_URL}/passkeys/{credentialId}`: revoke this credential for future authentication.
+
+All requests include `Authorization: Bearer <login token>`. The service must validate that token, scope reads and mutations to its owner, persist changes, and reject expired tokens with HTTP 401. Credential registration and WebAuthn authentication remain responsibilities of that service.
+
+Each successful request, including mutations, must return HTTP 200 with this full authoritative snapshot:
+
+```json
+{
+  "rpId": "your-app.example",
+  "user": { "id": "BASE64URL_WEBAUTHN_USER_HANDLE", "name": "reader", "displayName": "Reader" },
+  "passkeys": [
+    { "id": "BASE64URL_CREDENTIAL_ID", "displayName": "My laptop", "createdAt": "2026-11-08T12:00:00Z", "lastUsedAt": "2026-11-08T12:00:00Z" }
+  ]
+}
+```
+
+The RP ID must be valid for the app's origin. The user ID must be the original WebAuthn user handle, not the account's database ID. Never paginate or filter the credential list: `signalAllAcceptedCredentials` may hide credentials omitted from it. Return `passkeys: []` after the final key is removed.
+
+Supported browsers receive the full accepted list on load, refresh, rename, and removal using the [WebAuthn Signal API](https://www.w3.org/TR/webauthn-3/#sctn-signal). Failed or unsupported authenticator sync is shown separately from successful account changes. A per-key label is not the WebAuthn user display name; `signalCurrentUserDetails` is deliberately not used to rename individual keys. Browsers control their own passkey labels and may require users to manage those labels in device settings.
+
+Run focused checks with `node --test tests/passkeys.test.ts`, and compile with `pnpm run build`. No browser or running application server is required.
